# A passwd fixture for tests/greeter.sh. Three lines, each one a mistake the
# greeter's user filter can make — see shell/ui/greeter/GreeterFace.qml.
#
#   tester    a person: UID >= 1000, a real login shell, a GECOS display name
#             with the trailing empty fields a real passwd file carries
#
# ⚠️ THE HOME FIELDS ARE ALL /var/empty, and that is tests/no-secrets.sh
# doing its job: it refuses `/home/<name>` anywhere in the tree, and an
# invented account name in an invented path is still the shape it is looking
# for. The greeter reads name, uid, GECOS and shell; the home field is carried
# and never asserted, so nothing is lost by not writing one.
#   sysacct   a system account: UID below 1000, real shell. Kept out by UID.
#   noshell   UID >= 1000 but /sbin/nologin. Kept out by the shell test — this
#             is the one a UID-only filter would wrongly offer as a login.
#
# ⚠️ A COMMENT LINE IS PART OF THE FIXTURE, not decoration: /etc/passwd does not
# normally have one, and the parser must not turn it into a user. It has fewer
# than seven colon-separated fields, which is the guard that catches it.
tester:x:1000:1000:Test Person,,,:/var/empty:/bin/bash
sysacct:x:481:481:System Account:/var/lib/sysacct:/bin/bash
noshell:x:1001:1001:No Shell:/var/empty:/sbin/nologin
